ort header, and the filename slug.","The two-space blockquote indent style and formatSources' join behavior — do not widen scope to nearby export-formatting oddities; file separately if noticed.","On-screen citation rendering in the chat UI; this issue is export-only."],"risks":["The investigation could not grep the repo for other consumers: if any suite outside exportMarkdown.test.ts (e.g. a ChatArea or Sidebar component test) pins the buggy fallback strings, it must be updated in this PR; investigation confirmed no such pin exists inside exportMarkdown.test.ts itself.","The exported Markdown's rendered shape changes (fallback entries become proper list items instead of lazy continuations of the previous item) — that is the intended fix, but a reviewer should eyeball one exported file.","RED-loop visibility: acceptance tests should use value-printing matchers such as expect(result).toContain('> \"Relevant text\"') so the failing output shows the promised symptom; whole-string toBe diffs escape the inner double quotes and bare boolean assertions print no value (investigation test-writer guidance)."],"summary":"Fix the three fallback return paths of formatCitation in app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.ts so every fallback emits the leading '- ' list marker and the quoted transcript snippet blockquote ('> \"<snippet>\"'): the two YouTube fallbacks (unparseable video_url; URL that parses but has no 'v' parameter) currently return 'Test Video (timestamp link unavailable) — 0:10–0:20' with both the snippet and the '- ' marker dropped, and the Dynamous empty-lesson_url fallback keeps the snippet but lacks the marker. The fix ships with new acceptance cases added to the existing app/frontend/src/lib/exportMarkdown.test.ts; every current case must keep passing, including the exact console.warn assertion.","version":"2.0"},"sha256":"637f39f5e928c262d493c3fc8ba2678e7484beeda03bdb1e31b3dd619c42c602","source":"task-contract.json"},"design":{"content":{"ac_mapping":{"AC-1":["ap